Implement user story SKY-004-impl: Implement Express REST API server with /health, /search, /cheapest, and static dashboard

## Story Description
Create src/server.ts with Express app exporting named `app`, guarded listen(), and all four routes. Create src/public/index.html as a styled dashboard SPA. Configure package.json build/start scripts including public/ asset copying to dist/. Depends on SKY-002 for SkyscannerClient and FlightResult type.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports named `app` (Express instance) separately from `listen()` call, which is guarded by main-module check matching the output format (ESM or CJS) so tests never bind a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> } regardless of RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type text/html, body equal to contents of src/public/index.html read at runtime via fs.readFileSync (not hardcoded inline), never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- src/public/index.html is a styled dashboard: blue (#1a73e8) header with 'Skyscanner Dashboard' title and subtitle, centered card (max-width ~700px) with 2-column grid search form (from, to, date, adults with labels), search button, status area (error/empty/success), client-side JS calling GET /search and rendering results without page reload
- GET /search with valid params returns 200 { flights: FlightResult[], count, searchedAt } where count === flights.length and searchedAt is ISO-8601 distinct per request; adults defaults to 1 if absent; returns 400 { error } if required params missing or adults non-numeric
- GET /cheapest with valid params returns 200 with cheapest FlightResult (price ≤ all others); adults defaults to 1; returns 404 { error } if no flights found; returns 400 { error } if required params missing
- RAPIDAPI_KEY absent at startup → /search and /cheapest return 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; SkyscannerClient throws → 500 { error: string } without crash/unhandled rejection; FlightResult type imported from SKY-002 export, not redeclared inline
- package.json: 'start' → 'node dist/server.js'; 'build' produces dist/server.js and copies src/public/ to dist/public/; supertest + @types/supertest in devDependencies; `npx tsc --noEmit` exits 0





